trong USP capacity is the largest constant $C$C such that there exist strong USPs of size $(C-o(1))^k$(C−o(1))k and width $k$k for infinitely many values of $k$k. The USP capacity equals $3/2^{2/3}$3/2 2/3.\n\nStrong USP capacity conjecture. The strong USP capacity equals\n\n$$3/2^{2/3}.$$3/2 2/3.\n\nThis would show that strong USPs attain the same asymptotic capacity as USPs and, via the associated group-theoretic construction, would yield matrix multiplication exponent $\\omega=2$ω=2. The paper gives a lower bound of $2^{2/3}$2 2/3 for the strong USP capacity but no matching upper bound beyond the general USP-capacity bound.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nHenry Cohn, Robert Kleinberg, Balazs Szegedy and Christopher Umans, “Group-theoretic algorithms for matrix multiplication”, arXiv:math/0511460 (2005).\n\ncombinatoricsgroup-theorymatrix-multiplication\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSimultaneous double product property conjecture for abelian groups | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/379386/simultaneous-double-product-property-conjecture-for-abelian)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; If true, this would provide the algebraic route to the optimal matrix multiplication exponent $\\omega=2$ω=2. ... Henry Cohn, Robert Kleinberg, Balazs Szegedy and Christopher Umans, “Group-theoretic algorithms for matrix multiplication”, arXiv:math/0511460 (2005).\n\n# Simultaneous double product property conjecture for abelian groups\n\nStatus\n    open\n\nImportance\n    Research corpus\n\nSolutions\n    0\n\nAt least 20 years old · documented by 2005\n\nLet $n$n be a positive integer. A collection of pairs of subsets $A_i,B_i$A i​,B i​ of an abelian group $H$H satisfies the simultaneous double product property when the pairs satisfy the double product property and the corresponding difference-set disjointness conditions described in the paper. The parameters are measured by $|H|$∣H∣ and the products $|A_i||B_i|$∣A i​∣∣B i​∣.\n\nSimultaneous double product property conjecture. For arbitrarily large $n$n, there exists an abelian group $H$H with $n$n pairs of subsets $A_i,B_i$A i​,B i​ satisfying the simultaneous double product property such that\n\n$$|H|=n^{2+o(1)}$$∣H∣=n 2+o(1)\n\nand\n\n$$|A_i||B_i|\\ge n^{2-o(1)}.$$∣A i​∣∣B i​∣≥n 2−o(1).\n\nIf true, this would provide the algebraic route to the optimal matrix multiplication exponent $\\omega=2$ω=2. The preceding parameter bounds show that $\\alpha=\\beta=2$α=β=2 is the only possible way to achieve this exponent; existence of such families remains open.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nHenry Cohn, Robert Kleinberg, Balazs Szegedy and Christopher Umans, “Group-theoretic algorithms for matrix multiplication”, arXiv:math/0511460 (2005).\n\nabelian-groupsadditive-combinatoricsmatrix-multiplication\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCohn's SDPP conjecture for abelian groups | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/359855/cohn-s-sdpp-conjecture-for-abelian-groups)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; The conjecture is motivated by the goal of obtaining matrix-multiplication exponent $\\omega=2$ω=2 through SDPP constructions in abelian groups. ... Kevin Pratt, “On generalized corners and matrix multiplication”, arXiv:2309.03878 (2023).\n\n# Cohn's SDPP conjecture for abelian groups\n\nStatus\n    open\n\nImportance\n    Research corpus\n\nSolutions\n    0\n\nAt least 2 years old · documented by 2023\n\nLet $G$G be a finite abelian group, and let $(A_i,B_i)_{i=1}^n$(A i​,B i​)i=1 n​ be pairs of subsets satisfying the simultaneous double product property (SDPP): for each $i$i, the equation $aa'^{-1}=bb'^{-1}$a a′−1=b b′−1 has only the solution $a=a'$a=a′ and $b=b'$b=b′ for $a,a'\\in A_i$a,a′∈A i​ and $b,b'\\in B_i$b,b′∈B i​, and $a_i(a_j')^{-1}b_j(b_k')^{-1}=1$a i​(a j′​)−1 b j​(b k′​)−1=1 implies $i=k$i=k. Cohn's SDPP conjecture. For arbitrarily large $n$n, there exists an abelian group $G$G with\n\n$$|G|=n^{2-o(1)}$$∣G∣=n 2−o(1)\n\nand $n$n pairs of sets $A_i,B_i$A i​,B i​ satisfying the SDPP such that\n\n$$|A_i||B_i|>n^{2-o(1)}.$$∣A i​∣∣B i​∣>n 2−o(1).\n\nThe conjecture is motivated by the goal of obtaining matrix-multiplication exponent $\\omega=2$ω=2 through SDPP constructions in abelian groups. It is presented here as an external conjecture, with no resolution supplied in the source.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nKevin Pratt, “On generalized corners and matrix multiplication”, arXiv:2309.03878 (2023).\n\nadditive-combinatoricsfinite-groupsmatrix-multiplication\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nValiant's conjecture for iterated matrix multiplication — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/375152/valiant-s-conjecture-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; algebraic-complexity arithmetic-circuits matrix-multiplication\n\nValiant's conjecture for iterated matrix multiplication\n\nConjecture open\n\nLet $R$R be a field